Day 8 — AWS CloudTrail + Security & Compliance Logging

STAR-based DevOps Interview Questions

1️⃣ You need to track all API-level actions across multiple AWS accounts. How will you configure a multi-account CloudTrail setup?

2️⃣ A critical resource (IAM user, security group, EC2) was modified unexpectedly. How will you use CloudTrail to investigate the root cause?

3️⃣ Compliance requires storing logs for 7 years with immutability. How will you design CloudTrail + S3 + Glacier + Object Lock?

4️⃣ CloudTrail costs are increasing rapidly. What optimizations will you apply while maintaining security visibility?

5️⃣ You need near real-time alerts when suspicious actions occur (e.g., IAM policy changes). How will you integrate CloudTrail with EventBridge + SNS/Security Hub?

6️⃣ Your organization has separate dev, QA, and prod accounts. How will you centralize CloudTrail logs securely?

7️⃣ You must detect unauthorized access attempts. How will you design CloudTrail + GuardDuty integration?

8️⃣ CloudTrail logs are not showing events from S3 or Lambda. What configuration changes will you check?

9️⃣ A user denies performing a specific API call. How will you validate evidence using CloudTrail digest files?

🔟 You need to analyze CloudTrail logs for trends and anomalies. Which AWS analytics services will you use?

1️⃣1️⃣ You suspect a compromised access key. How will CloudTrail help you determine what resources were affected?

1️⃣2️⃣ CloudTrail is creating duplicate events across multiple trails. How will you optimize the configuration?

1️⃣3️⃣ You must prevent anyone from deleting or modifying audit logs. How will you enforce log integrity and permissions?

1️⃣4️⃣ A partner organization needs read-only access to specific CloudTrail logs. How will you design fine-grained S3 + IAM access?

1️⃣5️⃣ You need to automate compliance checks for CIS/NIST security frameworks. How will you combine CloudTrail with AWS Config?
